Patch 51. After patch 50. Android only.

The SDK builds SDL with its power subsystem off on every platform (thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt,
SDL_POWER), so on Android SDL_GetPowerInfo always answers SDL_POWERSTATE_UNKNOWN, although SDL
has the code there (Android_JNI_GetPowerInfo, which asks the app's Java side for the battery's
state). An app cannot tell it runs on battery. SDL_POWER is now on when ANDROID is set, which
builds SDL_GetPowerInfo_Android into libSDL3.a; the desktop platforms keep it off, as before
(each reads its own power sources).

Test: configured for Android (NDK r30, arm64-v8a), SDL_POWER is ON in the cache and libSDL3.a
defines SDL_GetPowerInfo_Android; configured for Linux, SDL_POWER stays OFF. The codegen id is
unchanged (the file is not one of its inputs). On the POCO X7, Torchlight's OnBattery through
SDL_GetPowerInfo with `dumpsys battery unplug` and `reset`: the render agent's check.

diff --git a/thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt b/thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt
index c192ac2..c830b6e 100644
--- a/thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/thirdparty/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -285,7 +285,13 @@ endif()
 set(SDL_RENDER_VULKAN OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
 set(SDL_HAPTIC OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
 set(SDL_SENSOR OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
-set(SDL_POWER OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
+# Power: on Android only, where SDL reads the battery through the app's Java side (an app can
+# tell it runs on battery); the desktop platforms keep it off.
+if(ANDROID)
+    set(SDL_POWER ON CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
+else()
+    set(SDL_POWER OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
+endif()
 set(SDL_FILESYSTEM OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
 set(SDL_LOCALE ON CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
 set(SDL_FILE OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
